IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc11-punishment`

-- ccc11-orders.l4 -- Part VIII.1, sections 320.23 to 320.25 (delay of sentencing; prohibition orders; stay pending appeal) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A power of the court ("may") whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12: a grant is not turned into a bar); a power whose gate is a where/when/upon-kind condition ("in the case of", "after considering", "with the consent of") answers the guide's JUST FALSE and is listed, not flipped (forks F34, F35); a duty, a bar and the provision's own question answer JUST FALSE
-- where the text's own "if" is unmet. Every power site is listed in the fork register (NOTES.md).

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.23: delay of sentencing`

-- The offences "under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)" are named by their place in the Code (R1). 320.14(1) takes in its paragraphs (a) to (d).
-- src:6305 | Delay of sentencing
-- src:6306 | 320.23 (1) The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the offender, and after considering the interests of justice, delay sentencing of an offender who has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1) to allow the offender to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which the offender resides. If the court delays sentencing, it shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question, in which case subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(1) (src:6305-6306)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` MEANS
    (offence's `section` EQUALS 320.14 AND (sub EQUALS "(1)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(a)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(b)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(c)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(d)"))
    OR (offence's `section` EQUALS 320.15 AND sub EQUALS "(1)")
    WHERE
        sub MEANS offence's `subsection`

-- "The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the offender, and after considering the interests of justice, delay sentencing ... to allow the offender to attend a treatment program
-- approved by the province": a power with no "if" gate: its conditions are "with the consent of the prosecutor and the offender" and "after considering the interests of justice" (a "with ... and after ..." gate, of the
-- where/when/upon kind: listed, not flipped, fork F34 in NOTES.md), so a consent not given or the interests of justice not considered answers the guide's JUST FALSE. The scope ("an offender who has been found guilty
-- of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)" and the purpose of the delay) is a scope limit with no "only": outside it the answer is NOTHING (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05). JUST FALSE beats NOTHING where both occur.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(1) (src:6305-6306)
GIVEN `the offender has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), by s 320.23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has considered the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delay is to allow the offender to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which the offender resides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the prosecutor consents`) OR (NOT `the offender consents`) OR (NOT `the court has considered the interests of justice`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the offender, and after considering the interests of justice, delay sentencing" (a gate of the with/after kind: listed, F34; the other reading is NOTHING)
    ELSE IF `the offender has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), by s 320.23(1)` AND `the delay is to allow the offender to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which the offender resides`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offender who has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1) to allow the offender to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which the offender resides"

-- Second sentence: "If the court delays sentencing, it shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question, in which case
-- subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply": a duty (JUST FALSE when the court has not delayed sentencing) and a rule of application.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(1) (src:6305-6306)
GIVEN `the court delays sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.23(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question` MEANS
    IF `the court delays sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court delays sentencing, it shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question" (the "if" unmet: the court has not delayed sentencing)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(1) (src:6305-6306)
GIVEN `the court has made an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.23(1) subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply to the order made before sentencing` MEANS
    IF `the court has made an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply" (the case unmet: no such order has been made)

DECLARE `s 320.23(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.23(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(1) (src:6305-6306)
GIVEN `the court delays sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.23(1) action`
`s 320.23(1) the court shall make a prohibition order before sentencing` MEANS
    IF `the court delays sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 320.23(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court delayed sentencing and did not make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 320.23(2): "If the offender successfully completes the treatment program, the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under
-- section 320.24, but it shall not direct a discharge under section 730." Two answers: the relief, and the bar on a discharge. Each is JUST FALSE where the "if" is unmet.
-- src:6307 | Exception to minimum punishment
-- src:6308 | (2) If the offender successfully completes the treatment program, the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24, but it shall not direct a discharge under section 730.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(2) (src:6307-6308)
GIVEN `the offender successfully completes the treatment program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.23(2) the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24` MEANS
    IF `the offender successfully completes the treatment program`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the offender successfully completes the treatment program, the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24" (the "if" unmet: this subsection gives no relief on these facts)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.23(2) (src:6307-6308)
GIVEN `the offender successfully completes the treatment program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.23(2) this subsection bars the court from directing a discharge under section 730` MEANS
    IF `the offender successfully completes the treatment program`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the offender successfully completes the treatment program, ... it shall not direct a discharge under section 730" (the "if" unmet: this subsection does not bar a discharge on these facts)

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.24: prohibition orders`

-- (1): the duty to make a prohibition order after a finding of guilt under 320.14(1) or 320.15(1): "the court that sentences the offender shall, in addition to any other punishment, make an order".
-- Subject to 320.23(2): where the offender has completed the treatment program the court "is not required" to make it (the answer of that subsection is an input).
-- src:6309 | Mandatory prohibition order
-- src:6310 | 320.24 (1) If an offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), the court that sentences the offender shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence, make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question during a period to be determined in accordance with subsection (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(1) (src:6309-6310)
GIVEN `the offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), by s 320.23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is not required to make a prohibition order, by s 320.23(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), by s 320.23(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), the court that sentences the offender shall, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence, make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question" (the "if" unmet)
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: the opposite of` `the court is not required to make a prohibition order, by s 320.23(2)`   -- JUST FALSE where 320.23(2) relieves the court: "the court is not required ... to make a prohibition order under section 320.24"
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

DECLARE `s 320.24(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.24(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(1) (src:6309-6310)
GIVEN `the offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.24(1) action`
`s 320.24(1) the court shall make a prohibition order` MEANS
    IF `the offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 320.24(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court that sentences the offender did not make the order that subsection 320.24(1) requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2): the prohibition period, by occasion: not less than one year and not more than three years (first), not less than two and not more than 10 (second), not less than three with no maximum
-- stated (subsequent), each "plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment". The period is a range, not a number, so it is a record.
DECLARE `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` HAS
    `s 320.24 not less than` IS A `Length of time`
    `s 320.24 not more than` IS A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
    `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6311 | Prohibition period
-- src:6312 | (2) The prohibition period is
-- src:6313 | (a) for a first offence, not less than one year and not more than three years, plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment;
-- src:6314 | (b) for a second offence, not less than two years and not more than 10 years, plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment; and
-- src:6315 | (c) for each subsequent offence, not less than three years, plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(2) (src:6311-6315)
GIVEN occasion IS A `s 320.19 occasion`
GIVETH A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` MEANS
    CONSIDER occasion
    WHEN `s 320.19 a first offence` THEN `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
        `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE
        `s 320.24 not more than` IS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)
        `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE
    WHEN `s 320.19 a second offence` THEN `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
        `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE
        `s 320.24 not more than` IS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)
        `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE
    WHEN `s 320.19 a subsequent offence` THEN `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
        `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE
        `s 320.24 not more than` IS NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (c) states "not less than three years" and no maximum
        `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE

-- (3): "may ... make an order prohibiting ... during a period of not more than one year" after a finding of guilt under 320.14(4): a power, answered with the longest period it may run.
-- The gate unmet answers NOTHING.
-- src:6316 | Discretionary order of prohibition — low blood drug concentration
-- src:6317 | (3) If an offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4), the court that sentences the offender may, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence, make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question during a period of not more than one year.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(3) (src:6316-6317)
GIVEN `the offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
`s 320.24(3) the longest period for which the court may prohibit the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` MEANS
    IF `the offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4)`
    THEN JUST (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an offender is found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4), the court that sentences the offender may, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence, make an order"

-- (4): the offences named by number: sections 220, 221, 236 and 320.13 (whole sections), subsections 320.14(2) and (3), 320.15(2) and (3), and sections 320.16 to 320.18 (whole sections; decimals sort
-- in the Code's order: 320.16, 320.17, 320.18). The power answers NOTHING outside the list (a power; the list is not closed with "only").
-- src:6318 | Discretionary order of prohibition — other offences
-- src:6319 | (4) If an offender is found guilty of an offence under section 220, 221, 236 or 320.13, subsection 320.14(2) or (3) or 320.15(2) or (3) or any of sections 320.16 to 320.18, the court that sentences the offender may, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence, make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question during a period to be determined in accordance with subsection (5).
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(4) (src:6318-6319)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` MEANS
    sec EQUALS 220 OR sec EQUALS 221 OR sec EQUALS 236 OR sec EQUALS 320.13
    OR (sec EQUALS 320.14 AND (sub EQUALS "(2)" OR sub EQUALS "(3)"))
    OR (sec EQUALS 320.15 AND (sub EQUALS "(2)" OR sub EQUALS "(3)"))
    OR (sec AT LEAST 320.16 AND sec AT MOST 320.18)
    WHERE
        sec MEANS offence's `section`
        sub MEANS offence's `subsection`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(4) (src:6318-6319)
GIVEN `the offender is found guilty of an offence listed in subsection 320.24(4), by s 320.24(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(4) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` MEANS
    IF `the offender is found guilty of an offence listed in subsection 320.24(4), by s 320.24(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an offender is found guilty of an offence under section 220, 221, 236 or 320.13, subsection 320.14(2) or (3) or 320.15(2) or (3) or any of sections 320.16 to 320.18, the court that sentences the offender may"

-- (5): the period, by the maximum imprisonment the offender is liable to for THAT offence (the offence sections state it: input, typed as the core types it): life -> any duration the court
-- considers appropriate (no maximum); more than five years but less than life -> not more than 10 years; any other case -> not more than three years; each plus the entire period of imprisonment.
-- No minimum is stated in any of the three: the minimum is the zero length.
-- src:6320 | Prohibition period
-- src:6321 | (5) The prohibition period is
-- src:6322 | (a) if the offender is liable to imprisonment for life in respect of that offence, of any duration that the court considers appropriate, plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment;
-- src:6323 | (b) if the offender is liable to imprisonment for more than five years but less than life in respect of that offence, not more than 10 years, plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment; and
-- src:6324 | (c) in any other case, not more than three years, plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(5) (src:6320-6324)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment the offender is liable to in respect of that offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment the offender is liable to in respect of that offence`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
        `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE
        `s 320.24 not more than` IS NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) is "of any duration that the court considers appropriate": no maximum is stated
        `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        IF term's years GREATER THAN 5 OR (term's years EQUALS 5 AND (term's months GREATER THAN 0 OR term's days GREATER THAN 0))
        THEN `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
            `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE
            `s 320.24 not more than` IS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)
            `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE
        ELSE `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
            `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE
            `s 320.24 not more than` IS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)
            `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN `s 320.24(2) prohibition period` WITH
        `s 320.24 not less than` IS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE
        `s 320.24 not more than` IS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)
        `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS TRUE

-- (5.1): "Subject to subsection (9), a prohibition order takes effect on the day that it is made." Where the court orders it served consecutively under (9), the text does not say on which day it then
-- takes effect: NOT COVERED.
-- src:6325 | Effect of order
-- src:6326 | (5.1) Subject to subsection (9), a prohibition order takes effect on the day that it is made.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(5.1) (src:6325-6326)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the court orders under subsection 320.24(9) that the order be served consecutively` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 320.24(5.1) the day on which the prohibition order takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the court orders under subsection 320.24(9) that the order be served consecutively`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Subject to subsection (9)": the text does not state the day a consecutive order takes effect
    ELSE JUST `the day on which the order is made`

-- (6): "A court that makes a prohibition order under this section shall cause the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender." A duty: JUST FALSE when no order is made.
-- src:6327 | Obligation of court
-- src:6328 | (6) A court that makes a prohibition order under this section shall cause the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(6) (src:6327-6328)
GIVEN `the court makes a prohibition order under section 320.24` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court causes the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(6) the court has met its obligation to cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court makes a prohibition order under section 320.24`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court that makes a prohibition order under this section shall cause the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender" (no order made: the obligation does not arise)
    ELSE JUST (`the court causes the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender`)

DECLARE `s 320.24(6) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.24(6) cause the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(6) (src:6327-6328)
GIVEN `the court makes a prohibition order under section 320.24` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.24(6) action`
`s 320.24(6) the court shall cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a prohibition order under section 320.24`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 320.24(6) cause the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not cause the order to be read or a copy to be given to the offender"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (7): "A failure to comply with subsection (6) does not affect the validity of the prohibition order." Asks whether the failure affects the validity: JUST FALSE where the court failed to comply.
-- src:6329 | Validity of prohibition order not affected
-- src:6330 | (7) A failure to comply with subsection (6) does not affect the validity of the prohibition order.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(7) (src:6329-6330)
GIVEN `the court failed to comply with subsection 320.24(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(7) a failure to comply with subsection 320.24(6) affects the validity of the prohibition order` MEANS
    IF `the court failed to comply with subsection 320.24(6)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A failure to comply with subsection (6) does not affect the validity of the prohibition order"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply with subsection (6)

-- (8): "A prohibition order in respect of a motor vehicle applies only to its operation on a street, road or highway or in any other public place." Closed with "only": JUST FALSE outside.
-- src:6331 | Application — public place
-- src:6332 | (8) A prohibition order in respect of a motor vehicle applies only to its operation on a street, road or highway or in any other public place.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(8) (src:6331-6332)
GIVEN `the order is in respect of a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the operation is on a street, road or highway or in any other public place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(8) the prohibition order applies to the operation of the motor vehicle` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order is in respect of a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle`
    WHEN JUST isMotorVehicle THEN
        IF isMotorVehicle
        THEN (IF `the operation is on a street, road or highway or in any other public place`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies only to its operation on a street, road or highway or in any other public place"
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A prohibition order in respect of a motor vehicle applies only to"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the thing is a motor vehicle is not determined (s 2 "motor vehicle")

-- (9): "If the offender is, at the time of the commission of the offence, subject to an order made under this Act prohibiting the offender from operating a conveyance, a court that makes a prohibition
-- order under this section that prohibits the offender from operating the same type of conveyance may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to that order": a power.
-- src:6333 | Consecutive prohibition periods
-- src:6334 | (9) If the offender is, at the time of the commission of the offence, subject to an order made under this Act prohibiting the offender from operating a conveyance, a court that makes a prohibition order under this section that prohibits the offender from operating the same type of conveyance may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to that order.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(9) (src:6333-6334)
GIVEN `at the time of the commission of the offence the offender was subject to an order made under this Act prohibiting the offender from operating a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new prohibition order prohibits the offender from operating the same type of conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(9) the court may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` MEANS
    IF `at the time of the commission of the offence the offender was subject to an order made under this Act prohibiting the offender from operating a conveyance` AND `the new prohibition order prohibits the offender from operating the same type of conveyance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the offender is, at the time of the commission of the offence, subject to an order made under this Act prohibiting the offender from operating a conveyance, a court that makes a prohibition order under this section that prohibits the offender from operating the same type of conveyance may order"

-- (10): "A person may not be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program referred to in subsection 320.18(2) until the expiry of (a) first offence: a period, if any, fixed by order of the
-- court; (b) second offence: three months after the day on which the sentence is imposed or any longer period fixed by order of the court; (c) subsequent offence: six months ... or any longer period fixed".
-- An "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE before the expiry, JUST FALSE from the day after. The period runs "after the day on which the sentence is imposed", so the bar is on through the whole of the day that
-- many months later (fork F11); months are added with `Date`, which rolls an impossible day forward (31 January + 3 months is 1 May).
-- src:6335 | Minimum absolute prohibition period
-- src:6336 | (10) A person may not be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program referred to in subsection 320.18(2) until the expiry of
-- src:6337 | (a) in the case of a first offence, a period, if any, that may be fixed by order of the court;
-- src:6338 | (b) in the case of a second offence, a period of three months after the day on which the sentence is imposed or any longer period that may be fixed by order of the court; and
-- src:6339 | (c) in the case of a subsequent offence, a period of six months after the day on which the sentence is imposed or any longer period that may be fixed by order of the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.24(10) (src:6335-6339)
GIVEN occasion IS A `s 320.19 occasion`
      `the day on which the sentence is imposed` IS A DATE
      `the period fixed by order of the court, in months, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` MEANS
    CONSIDER occasion
    WHEN `s 320.19 a first offence` THEN
        CONSIDER `the period fixed by order of the court, in months, if any`
        WHEN JUST fixed THEN JUST (`the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day of the bar` fixed)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a period, if any, that may be fixed by order of the court" (no period fixed: no bar)
    WHEN `s 320.19 a second offence` THEN JUST (`the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day of the bar` (`the longer of` 3 `the period fixed by order of the court, in months, if any`))
    WHEN `s 320.19 a subsequent offence` THEN JUST (`the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day of the bar` (`the longer of` 6 `the period fixed by order of the court, in months, if any`))
    WHERE
        `the last day of the bar` months MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `the day on which the sentence is imposed`) (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the sentence is imposed` PLUS months) (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the sentence is imposed`)
        `the longer of` statutory fixed MEANS
            CONSIDER fixed
            WHEN JUST f THEN IF f GREATER THAN statutory THEN f ELSE statutory
            WHEN NOTHING THEN statutory

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.25: stay of the prohibition order pending appeal`

-- (2): "In the case of an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, a direction may be made only by a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken": a gate of the "in the case of" kind (listed, not flipped,
-- fork F35 in NOTES.md), so on an appeal that is not to the Supreme Court of Canada the answer is the guide's JUST FALSE; and closed with "only", so in such an appeal a judge of any other court gets JUST FALSE too.
-- src:6342 | Appeals to Supreme Court of Canada
-- src:6343 | (2) In the case of an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, a direction may be made only by a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.25(2) (src:6342-6343)
GIVEN `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    IF NOT `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, a direction may be made only by a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken" (an "in the case of" gate: listed, F35; the other reading is NOTHING)
    ELSE IF `the judge is a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a direction may be made only by a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken"

-- (1): "Subject to subsection (2), if an appeal is taken against a conviction or sentence for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18, a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken may direct
-- that the prohibition order under section 320.24 arising out of the conviction shall, on any conditions that the judge imposes, be stayed pending the final disposition of the appeal or until otherwise ordered
-- by that court": a power with "if" gates. The gates unmet answer NOTHING; where subsection (2) closes the power (a Supreme Court of Canada appeal and a judge of the wrong court) the answer is its JUST FALSE.
-- Subsection (2) is consulted only on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada (it answers JUST FALSE for any other appeal, fork F35, which would otherwise close this power for every appeal).
-- src:6340 | Stay of order pending appeal
-- src:6341 | 320.25 (1) Subject to subsection (2), if an appeal is taken against a conviction or sentence for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18, a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken may direct that the prohibition order under section 320.24 arising out of the conviction shall, on any conditions that the judge imposes, be stayed pending the final disposition of the appeal or until otherwise ordered by that court.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.25(1) (src:6340-6341)
GIVEN `the offence is under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18, by s 320.22` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an appeal is taken against the conviction or the sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 320.25(2) allows this judge, by s 320.25(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.25(1) a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken may direct that the prohibition order be stayed pending the appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT `an appeal is taken against the conviction or the sentence`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if an appeal is taken against a conviction or sentence for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence is under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18, by s 320.22`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18"
         WHEN JUST inScope THEN
             IF NOT inScope
             THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18"
             ELSE CONSIDER (IF `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada` THEN `subsection 320.25(2) allows this judge, by s 320.25(2)` ELSE NOTHING)
                  WHEN JUST allowed THEN JUST allowed   -- JUST FALSE where subsection (2) says "only by a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken"
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN
                      IF `the judge is a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken may direct"

-- (3): "The imposition of conditions on a stay of a prohibition order does not operate to decrease the prohibition period provided in the prohibition order." Asks whether it decreases the period.
-- src:6344 | Effect of conditions
-- src:6345 | (3) The imposition of conditions on a stay of a prohibition order does not operate to decrease the prohibition period provided in the prohibition order.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.25(3) (src:6344-6345)
GIVEN `conditions are imposed on a stay of a prohibition order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.25(3) the imposition of conditions on a stay decreases the prohibition period` MEANS
    IF `conditions are imposed on a stay of a prohibition order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not operate to decrease the prohibition period provided in the prohibition order"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of conditions imposed on a stay
